A hash map stores values under keys.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    scores ~= {
        "Priya" = 10,
        "Rob" = 12,
    }
]

Use `get` to read a value:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    score = scores.get("Priya") catch:
        then 0
    ;
]

Use `set` and `remove` through a mutable receiver:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    ~scores.set("Emmy", 7) catch:
    ;

    removed = ~scores.remove("Rob") catch:
        then 0
    ;
]

Maps remember insertion order.

`length` is a property:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    count = scores.length
]

Builtin keys are `String`, `Int`, `Uint`, `Bool`, `Char`, every fixed-width integer and
`Byte`. Floats, `Dec` and `DecN` are not key types. Maps run on HTML-JS.
Wasm still rejects map runtime work. See @../progress (Progress) for current support.
